        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by the `HASH_OF_MAPS` implementation not properly releasing the inner map pointer during the `bpf_map_elem_update()` operation. This oversight occurred due to the per-cpu extra elements optimization, which bypassed the cleanup logic in `free_htab_elem()`, leading to a memory leak as the inner map pointers were not being freed correctly.

